      "content": "1|Sightings of slime and black winged kobolds around the city are becoming all too common. [[The Seekers of the Vein]] are now defending themselves from a class action law suit. They have cut ties with the [[Ashen Shadow Society]] as it has become clear that the problem is too large to keep the public unaware. The task of dealing with the faceless hoards has fallen upon anyone willing to take it up. Adventurers from all across [[Stickyickistan]] and beyond have now been venturing into the scrapyard in hopes of being the ones to find the source of the blight. Many denizens of the city have been increasingly reporting sightings of what looks like a giant flying serpentine puddle of murky liquid in the skies above the city. Another alarming occurrence since the arrest of [[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]] is the arrival of a mysterious individual in [[The Undercity Osslurraggath]] who calls himself \"The Blurry One\" . The Blurry One claims to be the harbinger of the slimy incursion who is returning to the city from the Abyss to claim vengeance on his killers. Locals claim to be able to faintly hear what they often describe as \"nostalgic melodies\" from the sewers at night.\n2|\n3|The trial of [[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]] is complete. Their sentences vary in length, but the judge made sure to throw the book at all of them. They have been labelled as dangers to society for various reasons, and therefore will be shipped over 1000 miles away to the infamous [[Giantfrost Penitentiary]] near the north pole of [[Mythmos]]. [[Ashen Shadow Society Creature Utilisation & Neutralisation Taskforce|ASSCUNT]] needs to make sure this does not happen. They have come up with a plan to intercept the airship meant to ship the prisoners out of the city, which is known as The Recluse. A Raven rank squad has been assigned to this extraction mission where they will be flown on a society owned airship to board the recluse with the prisoners on board, and release them, but they will need some help. [[Ashen Shadow Society|ASS]] has requested that the [[Heist Squad]] assist the Raven squad by infiltrating the [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition|THC]] guards assigned to the flight on The Recluse. Once the Raven squad has boarded The Recluse, and apprehended the captain, the Heist Squad should activate to release the prisoners using what info they have gained through being undercover. If all goes well, no one will die, and [[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]] will be brought back to the [[Ashen Citadel]] where they will be transitioned into the [[Ashen Shadow Society's Protected Outlaw Operatives Program]], aka A.S.S.P.O.O.P.\n4|\n5|# Infiltrating the THC\n6|\n7|\n8|",
