      "content": "7|## Joining the THC Detail\n8|\n9|[[Ashen Shadow Society]] handler **Merrick \"Moth\" Vane** has sent word to one of his field agents, **Nessa Bramblewick**, a chaotic good dwarf [[spy]]. Nessa meets the characters in [[Stickyickistan]] and provides uniforms, badges, and forged transfer orders for their chosen cover identities. The characters are replacing members of the [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition|THC]] detail assigned to escort [[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]] aboard [[The Recluse]]. Nessa directs them to report to the THC staging area before the airship's scheduled departure.\n10|\n11|The Recluse is preparing to carry the prisoners north to [[Giantfrost Penitentiary]]. The flight will take several days, giving the Heist Squad time to establish their covers, learn the ship's security procedures, and identify the best opportunity to help the Raven squad seize the vessel. Nessa warns them that their real allies will not reveal themselves until the operation is underway.\n12|\n13|Twenty-five guards and six cooks are assigned to The Recluse, including any characters taking their places. The cooks are not part of the formal security detail, but they have access to the crew areas, kitchens, stores, and service passages. If the characters express concern over the fate of staff they are replacing, Nessa assures them that the people were not killed and will be released safely once the extraction is complete.\n14|\n15|The players can make up whatever names they like for their cover identities. Those are the names of the THC guards or ship staff they have replaced. Nessa warns them that senior officers may know the original staff by sight, so the characters should avoid drawing attention to themselves until they have learned enough about their assumed identities.",
