      "content": "1|# ASSCUNT\n2|\n3|**Abbreviation:** ASSCUNT  \n4|**Parent Organization:** [[Ashen Shadow Society]]  \n5|**Director:** [[Kezrin Malvek]]  \n6|**Headquarters:** [[Ashen Citadel]]\n7|\n8|The **Ashen Shadow Society Creature Utilisation & Neutralisation Taskforce**, commonly shortened to **ASSCUNT**, is a specialized subsidiary of the [[Ashen Shadow Society]] dedicated to the capture, study, harvesting, and neutralization of dangerous creatures.\n9|\n10|Unlike ordinary bounty-hunting squads, ASSCUNT teams are expected to recover more than a target’s head or corpse. Monster organs, venom, magical glands, bones, hides, chitin, blood, mutagenic fluids, and other useful components are catalogued and delivered to the Society’s researchers. The taskforce exists to turn the dangers of [[The Outback]] and the wider multiverse into equipment, weapons, medicines, arcane components, and profitable research.\n11|\n12|## Purpose and Mandate\n13|\n14|ASSCUNT operates under a dual mandate:\n15|\n16|1. **Utilisation:** Recover valuable biological and magical components from monsters and other dangerous creatures.\n17|2. **Neutralisation:** Eliminate or contain creatures that threaten [[Stickyickistan]], the [[Ashen Shadow Society]], or the Society’s clients.\n18|\n19|The taskforce also investigates unusual specimens, tracks invasive creatures, escorts researchers into hostile environments, and secures sites containing dangerous remains or unstable biomantic materials. A mission may begin as a routine bounty and become an excavation, containment operation, salvage expedition, or field experiment.\n20|\n21|## Operations\n22|\n23|ASSCUNT squads are often assigned targets that ordinary hunters consider too strange, dangerous, or difficult to process. They may be sent to recover a single rare organ, clear a creature from a settlement, investigate a monster outbreak, or retrieve biological material before a rival faction finds it.\n24|\n25|Recovered components are transported to the [[Ashen Citadel]], where they are sorted, preserved, and distributed. Some materials are sold to approved clients. Others are sent to the Citadel’s forges, laboratories, alchemical facilities, or biomantic researchers. Particularly hazardous specimens are held in containment until they can be destroyed or studied safely.\n26|\n27|The taskforce maintains working relationships with the Society’s pilots, handlers, researchers, armorers, and information specialists. It also has reasons to monitor industrial sites such as [[Seekers' Scrapyard]], where discarded [[Magitech]], alchemical waste, and monster remains can attract opportunistic creatures.\n28|\n29|## Field Protocols\n30|",
