      "content": "117|# Adventure Conversion\n118|\n119|## Halfling Overboard\n120|\n121|It wasn’t long before the Strider Airship, _Recluse_, having departed the dwarven city of Soldorakhold only the day before, was beset by a group of human pirates aboard a pair of Lyrandar Skyskiffs as they passed over the vast Ironroot Mountains. See [chapter 7](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/efota/elemental-airships) of _[Eberron: Forge of the Artificer](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/efota)_ for the [Strider Airship](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/efota/elemental-airships#StriderAirship) and [Lyrandar Skyskiff](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/efota/elemental-airships#LyrandarSkyskiff) statistics.\n122|\n123|Eight pirates boarded the _Recluse_ when the _Recluse’s_ captain, a halfling named Ryvan Rallanith, made a brash decision; he veered the ship into a steep dive. Four of the pirates fell overboard—however, not before one of them cut the harnesses lashing Captain Rallanith to the helm. Four pirates remain aboard the airship.\n124|\n125|The soarwood planks of the ship groan and creak in protest as the Recluse hangs helplessly in the sky, the bow pitching steeply. Thousands of galifars’ worth of unsecured supplies and, more importantly, the halfling captain Ryvan Rallanith, are now black specks fading away hundreds of feet beneath.\n126|\n127|Kreffik Soldorak, your employer, lies in a heap of furniture and luggage nearby. “Dolurrh!” he cries out, pushing a small nightstand off himself and attempting to straighten out his coat, “what is that thrice-damned helmsman doing?!”\n128|\n129|Without a pilot, there’s no chance of the ship righting itself, let alone continuing their voyage."
    }
