      "nextStartLine": null,
      "content": "127|> [!read-aloud]\n128|> The grappling lines snap taut as the Raven operatives cross onto the deck. For one breath, the plan seems to be working. Then the captain wrenches the helm hard to one side. The Recluse plunges into a steep dive, and the entire ship groans around you. Crates, weapons, and bodies slide across the deck as the sky rushes up to meet you.\n129|>\n130|> With a sharp metallic crack, the captain cuts the harness holding him to the helm. The sudden release throws the Raven squad into open air, and the captain tumbles after them. One by one, their silhouettes vanish beneath the ship and into the clouds. The Society airship pulls away, leaving you alone aboard The Recluse with the prisoners, the THC, and a vessel that is still falling.\n131|\n132|\n133|The characters have only a short time before the surviving THC officers organize a response. If they act quickly, they can use the confusion to reach the prisoners and redirect The Recluse toward a rendezvous with the Society’s airship. If they delay, the guards seal the prisoner compartment, move the prisoners to a secondary holding area, and begin searching the ship for the intruders who helped the Raven squad board. The uncontrolled descent continues throughout the encounter, making every delay more dangerous.\n134|\n135|The Raven squad’s disappearance should not end the adventure. It removes the characters’ planned support and forces them to rely on the information, alliances, and access they gained while undercover. The extraction is still possible, but from this point forward, the Heist Squad is on its own aboard an airship that is rapidly approaching a catastrophic crash."
    }
